+    /// Paints one instance of a registered shader stretched over an arbitrary
+    /// convex quad, `corners` clockwise from the top-left, with the signals
+    /// and `meta` [`Window::paint_user_shader`] takes. `fs_user(uv)` gets a
+    /// perspective-correct 0..1 across the face.
+    ///
+    /// `resolution` and `mouse` belong to the quad's bounding box, not the
+    /// face. `mouse` stays bounds-local and untransformed, so a shader on a
+    /// tilted face reads the pointer in the box rather than on the face.
+    ///
+    /// Only a program that can run as the in-scene primitive paints here, one
